    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nMy first instinct is that screenshot tests should be used specifically if there is no way of writing test without them. Like for testing highlihgting, extmarks, command completion, UI, etc. Or if it would bring huge inconvenience (like too much text to put into file), but this is arguable.\r\n\r\nI do understand that having some \"compare to reference\" functionality might be useful. Like indeed something along the lines of `expect.reference_object(obj)` which saves `vim.inspect(obj)` on first run and then compares to the new `vim.inspect(obj)`. But currently I am on the fence about it. I'll think about it.",
