            "body": "> Probably cause you were using it without a neovim child? With a child, it only works for me if I do it inside the child, like:\r\n> \r\n> ```lua\r\n> child.lua([[vim.wait(...)]])\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n`vim.wait()` inside test runner process with callback using child process. Like [this](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/aa81e45b5977c1db3680c5ef4c016276cf1c7645/tests/test_diff.lua#L1123).",
