        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "As this issue hasn't reached a point when I'd feel adding the feature was a definite benefit, I am afraid I am going to close this. The reasoning is mostly the same as [in initial response](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/909#issuecomment-2127927701).\r\n\r\nPlus that implementing it would also require some careful consideration on what to do with objects that can not be converted to strings (like functions and userdata). The `vim.insepct()` approach of replacing them with `<function 1>` and `<userdata 1>` will not lead to a reliable \"compare with snapshot\" functionality.\r\n\r\nThanks for the suggestion, though, and for using 'mini.test'!",
